---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import type { CasePart } from "../types";
import setup from "./cockpit-participant-setup.png";
import display from "./cockpit-task-display.png";

interface Props {
  part: CasePart;
}
const { part } = Astro.props;
---

{part === "intro" && (
  <p>
    At the Institute of Software, Chinese Academy of Sciences, I developed a
    Unity directional-judgment task for an existing six-degree-of-freedom motion
    platform and analyzed response times.
  </p>
)}

{part === "visual" && (
  <figure class="portfolio-figure cockpit-apparatus">
    <div class="cockpit-photos">
      <figure class="cockpit-photo cockpit-photo-main">
        <Image
          src={setup}
          format="webp"
          widths={[414, 640, setup.width]}
          sizes="(min-width: 1000px) 640px, (min-width: 700px) 60vw, calc(100vw - 48px)"
          alt="Participant seated on the motion platform facing the task display, with the original face covering retained."
          width={setup.width}
          height={setup.height}
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
        <figcaption>Motion platform and participant.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cockpit-photo cockpit-photo-detail">
        <Image
          src={display}
          format="webp"
          widths={[320, display.width]}
          sizes="(min-width: 700px) 352px, calc(100vw - 48px)"
          alt="Task display showing a green directional arrow."
          width={display.width}
          height={display.height}
          loading="eager"
        />
        <figcaption>Directional cue on the task display.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      The study paired a physical motion platform with an on-screen directional
      task. Cropped from the original apparatus figure.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
)}

{part === "body" && (
  <>
    <p>
      Participants responded to an arrow using the corresponding directional
      key. Practice introduced the mapping with feedback; formal trials provided
      the behavioral records.
    </p>
    <h2>Commands and measurements</h2>
    <p>
      Commanding motion and measuring motion answer different questions. Unity
      specified the platform’s motion conditions, while sensors beneath the seat
      recorded the movement that occurred. Keeping these roles separate allowed
      the study to relate task performance to measured motion rather than
      treating a command setting as the measurement itself.
    </p>
    <h2>Task implementation</h2>
    <p>
      I implemented cue presentation and directional-response capture in Unity.
      The task emitted cue and response events alongside behavioral records,
      providing reference points for relating responses to the independent
      motion recordings.
    </p>

    <figure class="portfolio-figure cockpit-workflow">
      <div class="portfolio-diagram cockpit-map">
        <div class="cockpit-lanes">
          <section class="cockpit-lane" aria-labelledby="cockpit-task-lane">
            <h3 id="cockpit-task-lane">Task and events</h3>
            <div class="portfolio-node">
              <span class="cockpit-system">Unity environment</span>
              <strong>Directional task</strong>
              <span>Cue presentation · response capture</span>
            </div>
            <p class="cockpit-relationship">
              Emits <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
            </p>
            <div class="portfolio-node">
              <strong>Task records</strong>
              <span>Cue and response events</span>
              <span>Behavioral responses</span>
            </div>
          </section>
          <section class="cockpit-lane" aria-labelledby="cockpit-motion-lane">
            <h3 id="cockpit-motion-lane">Command and measurement</h3>
            <div class="portfolio-node">
              <span class="cockpit-system">Unity environment</span>
              <strong>Motion conditions</strong>
              <span>Platform-command output</span>
            </div>
            <p class="cockpit-relationship">
              Commands <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
            </p>
            <div class="portfolio-node">
              <strong>Physical motion platform</strong>
            </div>
            <p class="cockpit-relationship">
              Movement measured by <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
            </p>
            <div class="portfolio-node">
              <strong>Under-seat sensors</strong>
            </div>
            <p class="cockpit-relationship">
              Produce <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
            </p>
            <div class="portfolio-node">
              <strong>Independent motion records</strong>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
        <div class="cockpit-alignment portfolio-node">
          <span>Task records + motion records</span>
          <strong>Align for analysis</strong>
          <span>Motion relative to the cue direction</span>
        </div>

        <section class="cockpit-trial" aria-labelledby="cockpit-trial-heading">
          <h3 id="cockpit-trial-heading">Within each formal trial</h3>
          <ol class="cockpit-trial-sequence">
            <li>
              <strong>Fixation</strong>
            </li>
            <li class="cockpit-cue">
              <strong>Directional cue</strong>
              <span class="cockpit-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                ↑
              </span>
              <span>One of four directions</span>
              <span class="cockpit-response">Valid response recorded here</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Interval</strong>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p class="portfolio-note">
            The arrow remained visible for its scheduled interval; valid
            responses were recorded during that interval.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        Task events and physical measurements support a shared analysis. The
        inset shows the sequence within one trial; the main arrows indicate
        commands, events and measurements.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <details class="portfolio-methods">
      <summary>How motion was related to each cue</summary>
      <p>
        For each cue, motion was summarized over a fixed preceding interval and
        expressed relative to the direction of that cue. The window did not
        depend on how quickly the participant responded. This linked the
        definition of the behavioral task to the way motion was represented in
        the analysis.
      </p>
    </details>
  </>
)}

<style>
  .cockpit-apparatus {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .cockpit-photos {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
  }
  .cockpit-photo {
    margin: 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .cockpit-photo :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 0.7rem;
  }
  .cockpit-photo-main {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }
  .cockpit-photo-detail {
    max-width: 22rem;
  }
  .cockpit-photo figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.65rem;
  }
  .cockpit-map {
    padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 1.5rem);
  }
  .cockpit-lanes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }
  .cockpit-lane {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .cockpit-map h3 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .cockpit-map .portfolio-node {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
  .cockpit-system {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    color: var(--portfolio-accent);
  }
  .cockpit-relationship {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
    color: var(--portfolio-muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  .cockpit-relationship span {
    color: var(--portfolio-accent);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  .cockpit-alignment {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    border-color: var(--portfolio-accent);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .cockpit-trial {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .cockpit-trial-sequence {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.7fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.7rem;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .cockpit-trial-sequence li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.8rem 0.5rem;
    text-align: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
  }
  .cockpit-trial-sequence li::before {
    display: none;
  }
  .cockpit-trial-sequence li::marker {
    content: "";
  }
  .cockpit-trial-sequence strong {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .cockpit-trial-sequence span {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .cockpit-trial-sequence .cockpit-arrow {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    color: var(--portfolio-accent);
  }
  .cockpit-response {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .cockpit-trial .portfolio-note {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 699px) {
    .cockpit-photos {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .cockpit-photo-detail {
      width: min(100%, 22rem);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 479px) {
    .cockpit-map,
    .cockpit-map .portfolio-node {
      padding: 12px;
    }
    .cockpit-lanes {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
    .cockpit-trial-sequence {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .cockpit-trial-sequence li {
      padding: 12px;
    }
  }
</style>
